This package is a port of the `telemetry` package from pi
(https://github.com/earendil-works/pi), pinned at commit
8eb2bccf2603c28907ef3a583a04cafb1af284ae.

Provenance: this is a fork-and-adapt port, not a clean-room reimplementation.
The upstream sources were read directly and their structure, naming and
algorithms were carried across; the changes are the adaptations to this
repository's runtime and module layout, summarized below.

Adaptations, in order of how widely they apply:

  1. Relative specifiers no longer carry a `.ts` suffix, per this repository's
     `check-ts-relative-imports` invariant. Sixteen specifiers across the eight
     copied files.
  2. Barrels use star re-exports: `src/index.ts` re-exports `./noop` and
     `./memory` as stars, and `src/testing/index.ts` is two stars over
     `./conformance` and `./types`. The symbol sets are unchanged — the copied
     modules export 1 + 3 names and 3 + 1 names respectively — so this is a
     formatting change with no effect on what either entry point resolves.
  3. Class privacy: one field, `InMemoryTelemetryContext.state`, became an ES
     `#state` field, since AGENTS.md bans the `private` keyword. The public
     `startSpan` and `getSpans` methods stay bare.
  4. Tests moved from `vitest` to `bun:test`. No other vitest API was in use —
     no `vi`, no mocks, no globals — so this is the whole runner migration.
     `expectTypeOf` is provided by `bun:test`.

No `src/` file is byte-identical to its upstream counterpart, so none is listed
as copied verbatim.

Test assertions were replaced where the upstream form could not fail. Two
`expectTypeOf(compileTimeFailures).toBeFunction()` statements asserted only that
a function is a function; the contract they stood in for is the nine
`@ts-expect-error` comments inside those closures, which `tsgo` enforces, and
the bindings are kept so it keeps doing so. Five bare `not.toThrow()` statements
became assertions on observable results: the serialised schema is compared
against its exact JSON, a starter built from unreadable schemas is bound and a
later span is shown to still resolve, and the no-op context's callback returns a
sentinel that is asserted after each write call.

Added by this port, with no upstream counterpart: `LICENSE`, `NOTICE`,
`CHANGELOG.md`, `tsconfig.json` and `package.json` were rewritten for this
repository. Upstream's `tsconfig.build.json` was dropped — this repository sets
`noEmit` and forbids the `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json` build it served. The
version is `18.4.3`, this repository's release line; upstream's `0.87.1` is not
carried into the manifest.

